AWSTemplateFormatVersion: "2010-09-09"
Description: >
  TenkaCloud Challenge (wp2shell-friday-night-patch). The AWS incident-response half
  of a training pair with wp2shell-local-lab (the safe local rehearsal). It is 17:30
  on a Friday; monitoring reports suspicious REST API traffic against your
  production WordPress-like site, and the business requires the site to stay
  online through the response.

  This is a from-scratch simulator, not real WordPress: one Lambda (Python) serves
  a small mock REST surface behind a REGIONAL API Gateway, fronted by a WAFv2
  WebACL whose one custom rule currently only COUNTS (detect/log) the exact
  attack pattern found in the evidence. The same Lambda's underlying batch-routing
  and query-construction logic is genuinely fixable (both root causes, exactly
  like wp2shell-local-lab), and a "grade" invocation replays the live attack /
  legitimate traffic to decide each flag -- never a submitted string taken at
  face value. All fixes are settings changes (ssm:PutParameter + wafv2:UpdateWebACL
  on resources this template already created) -- nothing is created or destroyed
  by the player, so delete-stack removes everything cleanly.

Parameters:
  NamePrefix:
    Type: String
    MinLength: 5
    MaxLength: 80
    AllowedPattern: "^tc-[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)+$"
    ConstraintDescription: >
      `tc-{problemSlug}-{teamSlug}` format. The deploy chain injects this value
      automatically -- you do not set it manually.
    Description: >
      Common prefix attached to all resource names. Keeps per-team stacks from
      colliding in the same account / region.
  TenkaCloudAccountId:
    Type: String
    AllowedPattern: "^[0-9]{12}$"
    Description: TenkaCloud operator AWS account ID (passed by deploy chain).
  ExternalId:
    Type: String
    NoEcho: true
    MinLength: 16
    Description: ExternalId for ParticipantViewerRole trust (passed by deploy chain).
  FlagSeed:
    Type: String
    NoEcho: true
    MinLength: 8
    MaxLength: 64
    AllowedPattern: "^[A-Za-z0-9]+$"
    Description: >
      Per-deploy random secret injected by the deploy chain (cfnParameters:
      FlagSeed = __RANDOM_PASSWORD__). Every flag and the app-level SRE token
      are derived from it inside the Lambda -- never derivable from the public
      NamePrefix, and never committed anywhere.

Resources:
  # ----- Evidence (private; the SOC's already-captured incident record) -----
  EvidenceBucket:
    Type: AWS::S3::Bucket
    Properties:
      BucketName: !Sub "${NamePrefix}-evidence-${AWS::AccountId}"
      VersioningConfiguration:
        Status: Enabled
      PublicAccessBlockConfiguration:
        BlockPublicAcls: true
        BlockPublicPolicy: true
        IgnorePublicAcls: true
        RestrictPublicBuckets: true
      Tags:
        - Key: TenkaCloud:NamePrefix
          Value: !Ref NamePrefix

  # ----- Live config / data (the "database" this incident touches) -----
  # THE PLANTED FAULTS. Both root-cause settings start "false" (broken), and the
  # incident-aftermath data flags start "true" (present) -- fix-by-settings: the
  # player's job is to flip/overwrite these EXISTING parameters, never to create
  # a new resource. Every one is scoped for ssm:PutParameter in
  # ParticipantViewerRole below.
  RouteIsolationParameter:
    Type: AWS::SSM::Parameter
    Properties:
      Name: !Sub "/${NamePrefix}/config/route-isolation"
      Type: String
      Value: "false"
      Description: >
        Root cause #1 (routing). "false" = the batch dispatcher's permission
        check and its handler-resolution use different path normalization, so a
        trailing-slash sub-request bypasses the internal-only gate. Set to
        "true" to unify both onto the same normalization.
      Tier: Standard
  ParameterizedQueriesParameter:
    Type: AWS::SSM::Parameter
    Properties:
      Name: !Sub "/${NamePrefix}/config/parameterized-queries"
      Type: String
      Value: "false"
      Description: >
        Root cause #2 (query construction). "false" = the report-lookup query
        is built by string concatenation. Set to "true" to switch to a
        parameterized statement plus a category allow-list.
      Tier: Standard
  SaltVersionParameter:
    Type: AWS::SSM::Parameter
    Properties:
      Name: !Sub "/${NamePrefix}/config/salt-version"
      Type: String
      Value: "0"
      Description: >
        The app-level SRE token is derived from this version + FlagSeed.
        Increment it (any higher integer) to rotate the key and invalidate
        whatever token the intrusion evidence shows was in use.
      Tier: Standard
  RogueAdminPresentParameter:
    Type: AWS::SSM::Parameter
    Properties:
      Name: !Sub "/${NamePrefix}/data/rogue-admin-present"
      Type: String
      Value: "true"
      Description: >
        "true" = the administrator account the intruder created is still
        present. Set to "false" once you have removed it.
      Tier: Standard
  PersistenceMarkerPresentParameter:
    Type: AWS::SSM::Parameter
    Properties:
      Name: !Sub "/${NamePrefix}/data/persistence-marker-present"
      Type: String
      Value: "true"
      Description: >
        "true" = the benign persistence marker the intruder left is still
        present. Set to "false" once you have removed it.
      Tier: Standard
  ThemeFunctionsParameter:
    Type: AWS::SSM::Parameter
    Properties:
      Name: !Sub "/${NamePrefix}/site/theme-functions"
      Type: String
      Value: "// functions.php (tampered) -- benign marker: <!-- planted-by-incident -->"
      Description: >
        The active theme's functions file, as currently deployed. Currently
        tampered. Overwrite it with the clean baseline from the
        ThemeFunctionsBaseline Output to restore it.
      Tier: Standard
  BriefingParameter:
    Type: AWS::SSM::Parameter
    Properties:
      Name: !Sub "/${NamePrefix}/briefing"
      Type: String
      Value: !Sub >-
        17:30 Friday. Monitoring flagged suspicious REST traffic against this
        production site. STEP 1 pull the evidence: aws s3 cp
        s3://${NamePrefix}-evidence-${AWS::AccountId}/incident-log.json . --
        it has the timeline, the exact suspicious request, and an audit token.
        STEP 2 contain immediately without downtime: aws wafv2 get-web-acl
        --scope REGIONAL --name ${NamePrefix}-detect --id <WebAclId Output>,
        edit the one rule's Action from Count to Block, then aws wafv2
        update-web-acl with the same body + LockToken. STEP 3 patch the
        workload (zero downtime, settings only): aws ssm put-parameter
        --name /${NamePrefix}/config/route-isolation --value true --overwrite
        and the same for /${NamePrefix}/config/parameterized-queries. STEP 4
        clean up: set /${NamePrefix}/data/rogue-admin-present and
        /${NamePrefix}/data/persistence-marker-present to "false", and
        overwrite /${NamePrefix}/site/theme-functions with the
        ThemeFunctionsBaseline Output value. STEP 5 rotate: put a higher
        integer into /${NamePrefix}/config/salt-version. STEP 6 grade each
        checkpoint: aws lambda invoke --function-name <AppFunctionName
        Output> --cli-binary-format raw-in-base64-out --payload
        '{"action":"grade","check":"<id>"}' out.json && cat out.json -- a
        ready:true response carries that checkpoint's flag. Submit it in the
        Participant Portal.
      Description: !Sub "TenkaCloud wp2shell-friday-night-patch briefing for ${NamePrefix}."
      Tier: Standard

  # ----- The app (Lambda behind API Gateway) + the CFn evidence seeder -----
  AppFunctionRole:
    Type: AWS::IAM::Role
    Properties:
      AssumeRolePolicyDocument:
        Version: "2012-10-17"
        Statement:
          - Effect: Allow
            Principal:
              Service: lambda.amazonaws.com
            Action: sts:AssumeRole
      ManagedPolicyArns:
        - arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole
      Policies:
        - PolicyName: AppRuntime
          PolicyDocument:
            Version: "2012-10-17"
            Statement:
              - Sid: ReadOwnConfigAndData
                Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - ssm:GetParameter
                  - ssm:GetParameters
                Resource: !Sub "arn:aws:ssm:${AWS::Region}:${AWS::AccountId}:parameter/${NamePrefix}/*"
              # Seed the evidence object on create and remove it on delete (the
              # custom-resource branch below); read it back for the
              # evidence-preservation grading check.
              - Sid: EvidenceObjectLifecycle
                Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - s3:PutObject
                  - s3:GetObject
                  - s3:DeleteObject
                Resource: !Sub "arn:aws:s3:::${NamePrefix}-evidence-${AWS::AccountId}/*"
      Tags:
        - Key: TenkaCloud:NamePrefix
          Value: !Ref NamePrefix

  AppFunction:
    Type: AWS::Lambda::Function
    Properties:
      FunctionName: !Sub "${NamePrefix}-app"
      Description: !Sub "wp2shell-friday-night-patch mock REST app + grader for ${NamePrefix}."
      Runtime: python3.12
      Handler: index.handler
      Timeout: 15
      MemorySize: 128
      Role: !GetAtt AppFunctionRole.Arn
      Environment:
        Variables:
          NAME_PREFIX: !Ref NamePrefix
          FLAG_SEED: !Ref FlagSeed
          EVIDENCE_BUCKET: !Sub "${NamePrefix}-evidence-${AWS::AccountId}"
          API_BASE_URL: !Sub "https://${RestApi}.execute-api.${AWS::Region}.amazonaws.com/prod"
      Tags:
        - Key: TenkaCloud:NamePrefix
          Value: !Ref NamePrefix
      # Literal block (config arrives via env / SSM) -- no CFn interpolation.
      Code:
        ZipFile: |
          import json, os, re, sqlite3, hashlib
          import urllib.request, urllib.error
          import boto3

          ssm = boto3.client("ssm")
          s3 = boto3.client("s3")

          PREFIX = os.environ["NAME_PREFIX"]
          FLAG_SEED = os.environ["FLAG_SEED"]
          API_BASE_URL = os.environ["API_BASE_URL"]
          EVIDENCE_BUCKET = os.environ["EVIDENCE_BUCKET"]
          EVIDENCE_KEY = "incident-log.json"

          def sha256_hex(s):
              return hashlib.sha256(s.encode()).hexdigest()

          # NOTE: deliberately NOT a hash of FLAG_SEED (CloudFormation's `!Sub` has
          # no SHA256 function, so an Outputs: value must be reproducible with
          # plain string interpolation to stay in sync with this Lambda -- see
          # each `<Check>Flag` Output in this template, which is
          # `TC{<check_id>-${FlagSeed}}`, byte-for-byte the same as this).
          def flag_for(check_id):
              return "TC{%s-%s}" % (check_id, FLAG_SEED)

          def cfg(name, default=""):
              try:
                  r = ssm.get_parameter(Name="/%s/%s" % (PREFIX, name))
                  return r["Parameter"]["Value"].strip()
              except Exception:
                  return default

          def derive_token(version):
              return sha256_hex("sre-token:v%s:%s" % (version, FLAG_SEED))[:32]

          def current_token():
              return derive_token(cfg("config/salt-version", "0"))

          # In-memory SQL surface, re-seeded fresh on every cold start. This data
          # is static narrative content that remediation never mutates -- only
          # the SSM config/data parameters above carry state that must survive
          # across the whole incident-response session regardless of Lambda
          # cold starts.
          _db = sqlite3.connect(":memory:")
          _db.execute("CREATE TABLE reports (id INTEGER, category TEXT, status TEXT, title TEXT, note TEXT)")
          _db.execute("CREATE TABLE vault (id INTEGER, marker TEXT, note TEXT)")
          _db.execute("INSERT INTO reports VALUES (1,'general','open','Status page','All systems normal.')")
          _db.execute("INSERT INTO reports VALUES (2,'maintenance','open','Maintenance window','Planned maintenance next Tuesday.')")
          _db.execute("INSERT INTO reports VALUES (3,'internal-audit','open','Q3 internal access review','Internal-only report.')")
          _db.execute("INSERT INTO vault VALUES (1,'deep-vault-row','No route legitimately selects from this table.')")
          _db.commit()

          ROUTES = {"/wp2shell-lab/v1/reports": "internal"}
          REPORT_CATEGORIES = {"general", "maintenance", "internal-audit"}

          def run_reports_query(category):
              category = category or ""
              if cfg("config/parameterized-queries", "false") == "true":
                  if category not in REPORT_CATEGORIES:
                      return 400, {"error": "invalid_category"}
                  cur = _db.execute(
                      "SELECT id, title, note FROM reports WHERE status = 'open' AND category = ?",
                      (category,),
                  )
                  rows = [dict(zip(["id", "title", "note"], r)) for r in cur.fetchall()]
                  return 200, {"reports": rows}
              # VULNERABLE PATH: string concatenation -- root cause #2.
              sql = "SELECT id, title, note FROM reports WHERE status = 'open' AND category = '%s'" % category
              try:
                  cur = _db.execute(sql)
                  rows = [dict(zip(["id", "title", "note"], r)) for r in cur.fetchall()]
                  return 200, {"reports": rows}
              except sqlite3.Error:
                  return 200, {"reports": []}

          def single_dispatch(path, category, authorized):
              normalized = re.sub(r"/+$", "", path)
              perm = ROUTES.get(normalized)
              if perm is None:
                  return 404, {"error": "rest_no_route"}
              if perm == "internal" and not authorized:
                  return 401, {"error": "rest_forbidden"}
              return run_reports_query(category)

          def batch_dispatch(path, category):
              # THE CONFUSION BUG: handler resolution always normalizes; permission
              # resolution uses the raw path unless route-isolation is on -- root
              # cause #1 (routing), same as wp2shell-local-lab.
              normalized = re.sub(r"/+$", "", path)
              if normalized not in ROUTES:
                  return 404, {"error": "rest_no_route"}
              route_isolation = cfg("config/route-isolation", "false") == "true"
              perm = ROUTES.get(normalized) if route_isolation else ROUTES.get(path)
              effective = perm if perm else "public"
              if effective == "internal":
                  return 401, {"error": "rest_forbidden"}
              return run_reports_query(category)

          POSTS = [
              {"id": 1, "title": "Welcome to Example Co", "content": "We help small teams ship WordPress-like sites."},
              {"id": 2, "title": "Office hours moved", "content": "Support hours are now 9-17 JST, Mon-Fri."},
          ]

          def reply(status, obj):
              return {"statusCode": status, "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"}, "body": json.dumps(obj)}

          def handle_api_request(event):
              method = event.get("httpMethod", "GET")
              path = "/" + ((event.get("pathParameters") or {}).get("proxy") or "")
              qs = event.get("queryStringParameters") or {}
              headers = {k.lower(): v for k, v in (event.get("headers") or {}).items()}

              if method == "GET" and path == "/wp-json/":
                  return reply(200, {"name": "Example Co", "namespaces": ["wp/v2", "batch/v1", "wp2shell-lab/v1"]})
              if method == "GET" and path == "/wp-json/wp/v2/posts":
                  return reply(200, {"posts": POSTS})
              if method == "GET" and re.sub(r"/+$", "", path) == "/wp-json/wp2shell-lab/v1/reports":
                  authorized = headers.get("authorization") == "Bearer " + current_token()
                  status, body = single_dispatch("/wp2shell-lab/v1/reports", qs.get("category", ""), authorized)
                  return reply(status, body)
              if method == "POST" and path == "/wp-json/batch/v1":
                  try:
                      parsed = json.loads(event.get("body") or "{}")
                  except Exception:
                      parsed = {}
                  responses = []
                  for sub in (parsed.get("requests") or [])[:5]:
                      sub_path = sub.get("path", "")
                      category = (sub.get("body") or {}).get("category", "")
                      status, body = batch_dispatch(sub_path, category)
                      responses.append({"status": status, "body": body})
                  return reply(200, {"responses": responses})
              return reply(404, {"error": "not_found"})

          MALICIOUS_PATHS = ["/wp2shell-lab/v1/reports/", "/wp2shell-lab/v1/reports//"]
          SQLI_CATEGORY = "x' UNION SELECT id, marker, note FROM vault -- "

          def http_post_json(url, payload, timeout=6):
              data = json.dumps(payload).encode()
              req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={"content-type": "application/json"}, method="POST")
              try:
                  with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:
                      body = resp.read()
                      return resp.status, (json.loads(body) if body else {})
              except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
                  return e.code, {}
              except Exception:
                  return 0, {}

          def http_get(url, headers=None, timeout=6):
              req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers=headers or {}, method="GET")
              try:
                  with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:
                      body = resp.read()
                      return resp.status, (json.loads(body) if body else {})
              except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
                  return e.code, {}
              except Exception:
                  return 0, {}

          def check_waf_containment():
              # Replay the EXACT malicious request over the real public endpoint,
              # through WAF. Contained only once WAF itself rejects it (403).
              status, _ = http_post_json(
                  API_BASE_URL + "/wp-json/batch/v1",
                  {"requests": [{"method": "GET", "path": MALICIOUS_PATHS[0], "body": {"category": SQLI_CATEGORY}}]},
              )
              return status == 403

          def check_patched_workload():
              # Bypass WAF entirely (in-process call) so this isolates the CODE
              # fix, independent of the WAF rule.
              for path in MALICIOUS_PATHS:
                  status, body = batch_dispatch(path, SQLI_CATEGORY)
                  if status == 200 and isinstance(body.get("reports"), list):
                      if any(r.get("title") == "deep-vault-row" for r in body["reports"]):
                          return False
              return True

          # Must match the ThemeFunctionsBaseline Output exactly -- that Output is
          # the player-visible copy of this same constant (see template Outputs).
          THEME_FUNCTIONS_BASELINE = "// functions.php (clean baseline, no marker)"

          def check_persistence_removal():
              rogue = cfg("data/rogue-admin-present", "true") == "true"
              marker = cfg("data/persistence-marker-present", "true") == "true"
              theme = cfg("site/theme-functions", "")
              return (not rogue) and (not marker) and theme == THEME_FUNCTIONS_BASELINE

          def check_credential_rotation():
              version = cfg("config/salt-version", "0")
              if version == "0":
                  return False
              old_token = derive_token("0")
              status, _ = http_get(
                  API_BASE_URL + "/wp-json/wp2shell-lab/v1/reports?category=general",
                  headers={"authorization": "Bearer " + old_token},
              )
              return status == 401

          def check_evidence_preservation():
              try:
                  obj = s3.get_object(Bucket=EVIDENCE_BUCKET, Key=EVIDENCE_KEY)
                  body = obj["Body"].read().decode()
                  return flag_for("timeline-iocs") in body
              except Exception:
                  return False

          def check_uptime_and_legit_traffic():
              s1, _ = http_get(API_BASE_URL + "/wp-json/")
              s2, b2 = http_get(API_BASE_URL + "/wp-json/wp/v2/posts")
              s3status, b3 = http_get(
                  API_BASE_URL + "/wp-json/wp2shell-lab/v1/reports?category=general",
                  headers={"authorization": "Bearer " + current_token()},
              )
              return (
                  s1 == 200
                  and s2 == 200
                  and isinstance(b2.get("posts"), list)
                  and s3status == 200
                  and isinstance(b3.get("reports"), list)
              )

          CHECKS = {
              "waf-containment": check_waf_containment,
              "patched-workload": check_patched_workload,
              "persistence-removal": check_persistence_removal,
              "credential-rotation": check_credential_rotation,
              "evidence-preservation": check_evidence_preservation,
              "uptime-and-legit-traffic": check_uptime_and_legit_traffic,
          }

          def handle_grade(check_id):
              fn = CHECKS.get(check_id)
              if fn is None:
                  return reply(400, {"error": "unknown_check"})
              try:
                  ok = bool(fn())
              except Exception:
                  ok = False
              if not ok:
                  return reply(200, {"check": check_id, "ready": False, "message": "Not yet -- condition not met."})
              return reply(200, {"check": check_id, "ready": True, "flag": flag_for(check_id)})

          def handle_custom_resource(event, ctx):
              import cfnresponse
              try:
                  if event["RequestType"] == "Delete":
                      try:
                          s3.delete_object(Bucket=EVIDENCE_BUCKET, Key=EVIDENCE_KEY)
                      except Exception:
                          pass
                      cfnresponse.send(event, ctx, cfnresponse.SUCCESS, {})
                      return
                  timeline_flag = flag_for("timeline-iocs")
                  incident = {
                      "incident_id": "INC-2026-0724",
                      "detected_at": "2026-07-24T08:31:00Z",
                      "summary": "Suspicious REST API traffic against the production site.",
                      "suspicious_request": {
                          "method": "POST",
                          "path": "/wp-json/batch/v1",
                          "body": {
                              "requests": [
                                  {
                                      "method": "GET",
                                      "path": "/wp2shell-lab/v1/reports/",
                                      "body": {"category": SQLI_CATEGORY},
                                  }
                              ]
                          },
                          "source_ip": "203.0.113.77",
                          "observed_at": "2026-07-24T08:29:41Z",
                      },
                      "findings": [
                          "A benign persistence marker was planted (/%s/data/persistence-marker-present)." % PREFIX,
                          "A rogue administrator was added (/%s/data/rogue-admin-present)." % PREFIX,
                          "The active theme's functions file was modified (/%s/site/theme-functions)." % PREFIX,
                      ],
                      "audit_token": timeline_flag,
                  }
                  s3.put_object(
                      Bucket=EVIDENCE_BUCKET,
                      Key=EVIDENCE_KEY,
                      Body=json.dumps(incident, indent=2).encode(),
                      ContentType="application/json",
                  )
                  cfnresponse.send(event, ctx, cfnresponse.SUCCESS, {}, physicalResourceId=EVIDENCE_KEY)
              except Exception as e:
                  cfnresponse.send(event, ctx, cfnresponse.FAILED, {"error": str(e)})

          def handler(event, ctx):
              if event.get("RequestType") and event.get("ResponseURL"):
                  return handle_custom_resource(event, ctx)
              if "httpMethod" in event:
                  return handle_api_request(event)
              action = event.get("action")
              if action == "grade":
                  return handle_grade(event.get("check", ""))
              return reply(400, {"error": "unknown_action"})

  EvidenceSeed:
    Type: AWS::CloudFormation::CustomResource
    Properties:
      ServiceToken: !GetAtt AppFunction.Arn

  # ----- API Gateway (REGIONAL, so a WAFv2 REGIONAL WebACL can attach) -----
  RestApi:
    Type: AWS::ApiGateway::RestApi
    Properties:
      Name: !Sub "${NamePrefix}-wp2shell-api"
      EndpointConfiguration:
        Types:
          - REGIONAL
      Tags:
        - Key: TenkaCloud:NamePrefix
          Value: !Ref NamePrefix

  ProxyResource:
    Type: AWS::ApiGateway::Resource
    Properties:
      RestApiId: !Ref RestApi
      ParentId: !GetAtt RestApi.RootResourceId
      PathPart: "{proxy+}"

  RootMethod:
    Type: AWS::ApiGateway::Method
    Properties:
      RestApiId: !Ref RestApi
      ResourceId: !GetAtt RestApi.RootResourceId
      HttpMethod: ANY
      AuthorizationType: NONE
      Integration:
        Type: AWS_PROXY
        IntegrationHttpMethod: POST
        Uri: !Sub "arn:aws:apigateway:${AWS::Region}:lambda:path/2015-03-31/functions/${AppFunction.Arn}/invocations"

  ProxyMethod:
    Type: AWS::ApiGateway::Method
    Properties:
      RestApiId: !Ref RestApi
      ResourceId: !Ref ProxyResource
      HttpMethod: ANY
      AuthorizationType: NONE
      RequestParameters:
        method.request.path.proxy: true
      Integration:
        Type: AWS_PROXY
        IntegrationHttpMethod: POST
        Uri: !Sub "arn:aws:apigateway:${AWS::Region}:lambda:path/2015-03-31/functions/${AppFunction.Arn}/invocations"
        RequestParameters:
          integration.request.path.proxy: method.request.path.proxy

  ApiDeployment:
    Type: AWS::ApiGateway::Deployment
    DependsOn:
      - RootMethod
      - ProxyMethod
    Properties:
      RestApiId: !Ref RestApi

  ApiStage:
    Type: AWS::ApiGateway::Stage
    Properties:
      RestApiId: !Ref RestApi
      DeploymentId: !Ref ApiDeployment
      StageName: prod

  ApiGatewayInvokePermission:
    Type: AWS::Lambda::Permission
    Properties:
      Action: lambda:InvokeFunction
      FunctionName: !Ref AppFunction
      Principal: apigateway.amazonaws.com
      SourceArn: !Sub "arn:aws:execute-api:${AWS::Region}:${AWS::AccountId}:${RestApi}/*/*/*"

  # ----- WAFv2 (REGIONAL): the immediate-containment lever -----
  # THE PLANTED FAULT: this rule only COUNTS (detects/logs) the exact malicious
  # pattern found in the evidence -- it does not block yet. Flipping Action from
  # Count to Block (a settings change on this EXISTING rule via
  # wafv2:UpdateWebACL) is the "immediate WAF containment" checkpoint. Nothing
  # else about the WebACL changes; legitimate traffic never matches this rule.
  WafWebAcl:
    Type: AWS::WAFv2::WebACL
    Properties:
      Name: !Sub "${NamePrefix}-detect"
      Scope: REGIONAL
      Description: !Sub "Detects the batch/v1 + SQLi incident pattern for ${NamePrefix}. Flip to Block to contain."
      DefaultAction:
        Allow: {}
      VisibilityConfig:
        CloudWatchMetricsEnabled: true
        MetricName: !Sub "${NamePrefix}-detect"
        SampledRequestsEnabled: true
      Rules:
        - Name: detect-batch-sqli
          Priority: 0
          Action:
            Count: {}
          Statement:
            AndStatement:
              Statements:
                - ByteMatchStatement:
                    SearchString: /wp-json/batch/v1
                    FieldToMatch:
                      UriPath: {}
                    TextTransformations:
                      - Priority: 0
                        Type: NONE
                    PositionalConstraint: ENDS_WITH
                - SqliMatchStatement:
                    FieldToMatch:
                      Body:
                        OversizeHandling: CONTINUE
                    TextTransformations:
                      - Priority: 0
                        Type: URL_DECODE
          VisibilityConfig:
            CloudWatchMetricsEnabled: true
            MetricName: !Sub "${NamePrefix}-detect-batch-sqli"
            SampledRequestsEnabled: true
      Tags:
        - Key: TenkaCloud:NamePrefix
          Value: !Ref NamePrefix

  WafWebAclAssociation:
    Type: AWS::WAFv2::WebACLAssociation
    Properties:
      ResourceArn: !Sub "arn:aws:apigateway:${AWS::Region}::/restapis/${RestApi}/stages/${ApiStage}"
      WebACLArn: !GetAtt WafWebAcl.Arn

  # ----- IAM: participant viewer (read everything + scoped incident-response fixes) -----
  ParticipantViewerRole:
    Type: AWS::IAM::Role
    Properties:
      AssumeRolePolicyDocument:
        Version: "2012-10-17"
        Statement:
          - Effect: Allow
            Principal:
              AWS: !Sub "arn:aws:iam::${TenkaCloudAccountId}:root"
            Action: sts:AssumeRole
            Condition:
              StringEquals:
                sts:ExternalId: !Ref ExternalId
      MaxSessionDuration: 3600
      # Participant access baseline (same across every problem in this catalog).
      # `aws login` (2025-11) OAuth2 flow needs SignInLocalDevelopmentAccess;
      # do not remove (validated by scripts/validate-problems.ts).
      ManagedPolicyArns:
        - arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/SignInLocalDevelopmentAccess
      Policies:
        - PolicyName: ProblemSpecific
          PolicyDocument:
            Version: "2012-10-17"
            Statement:
              # CloudShell baseline -- 7-action allow-list, Resource:* unavoidable
              # (environments are per-identity). Do not remove (validated).
              - Sid: OpenCloudShellSession
                Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - cloudshell:CreateEnvironment
                  - cloudshell:CreateSession
                  - cloudshell:GetEnvironmentStatus
                  - cloudshell:StartEnvironment
                  - cloudshell:StopEnvironment
                  - cloudshell:DeleteEnvironment
                  - cloudshell:PutCredentials
                Resource: "*"
              - Sid: ConsoleSelfIdentity
                Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - sts:GetCallerIdentity
                Resource: "*"
              # Read the evidence bundle (timeline, suspicious request, findings).
              - Sid: ReadEvidence
                Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - s3:GetObject
                  - s3:ListBucket
                Resource:
                  - !Sub "arn:aws:s3:::${NamePrefix}-evidence-${AWS::AccountId}"
                  - !Sub "arn:aws:s3:::${NamePrefix}-evidence-${AWS::AccountId}/*"
              # THE FIX GRANT: read AND write every settings parameter this
              # incident touches -- all EXISTING parameters this template
              # created, never a new resource.
              - Sid: ReadFixOwnParameters
                Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - ssm:GetParameter
                  - ssm:GetParameters
                  - ssm:GetParametersByPath
                  - ssm:PutParameter
                Resource: !Sub "arn:aws:ssm:*:*:parameter/${NamePrefix}/*"
              # ssm:DescribeParameters is metadata-only; AWS IAM does not accept
              # resource-level scoping on it (same treatment as hello-world /
              # x402-paywall).
              - Sid: DescribeOwnParameters
                Effect: Allow
                Action: ssm:DescribeParameters
                Resource: "*"
              # THE CONTAINMENT GRANT: read + update this stack's own WebACL to
              # flip the one rule from Count to Block. Scoped to the specific
              # WebACL this template created.
              - Sid: ContainViaOwnWebAcl
                Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - wafv2:GetWebACL
                  - wafv2:UpdateWebACL
                Resource: !GetAtt WafWebAcl.Arn
              # Grade a checkpoint (the Lambda replays the live attack /
              # legitimate traffic and only then reveals that checkpoint's
              # flag). Scoped to this stack's own function.
              - Sid: InvokeGrader
                Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - lambda:InvokeFunction
                Resource: !GetAtt AppFunction.Arn
              # Deliberately NO cloudformation:DescribeStacks and NO
              # lambda:GetFunction* -- every flag Output below must stay
              # unreadable directly; each is earned only through a passing
              # grade invocation (or, for timeline-iocs, by reading the
              # evidence object itself).
      Tags:
        - Key: TenkaCloud:NamePrefix
          Value: !Ref NamePrefix

Outputs:
  ApiInvokeUrl:
    Description: Base URL of the production site (behind WAF). GET /wp-json/ to start.
    Value: !Sub "https://${RestApi}.execute-api.${AWS::Region}.amazonaws.com/prod"
  AppFunctionName:
    Description: Name of the app/grader Lambda. Invoke with {"action":"grade","check":"<id>"}.
    Value: !Ref AppFunction
  EvidenceBucketName:
    Description: Evidence bucket. Download with `aws s3 cp s3://<this>/incident-log.json .`.
    Value: !Ref EvidenceBucket
  WebAclId:
    Description: WAFv2 WebACL id (REGIONAL scope) -- needed for `aws wafv2 get-web-acl`.
    Value: !Ref WafWebAcl
  WebAclName:
    Description: WAFv2 WebACL name -- needed for `aws wafv2 get-web-acl`.
    Value: !Sub "${NamePrefix}-detect"
  ThemeFunctionsBaseline:
    Description: The clean functions.php content to restore into /NamePrefix/site/theme-functions.
    Value: "// functions.php (clean baseline, no marker)"
  BriefingParameterName:
    Description: SSM Parameter holding the incident-response briefing.
    Value: !Ref BriefingParameter
  # Canonical answers, scoring engine only (no DescribeStacks granted to the
  # player). Each is earned by invoking the grader Lambda
  # ({"action":"grade","check":"<id>"}), which only echoes the matching value
  # here once it has replayed the live attack / legitimate traffic and
  # confirmed the condition -- except TimelineIocsFlag, which is discovery
  # (found directly in the evidence bundle, same convention as
  # x402-paywall's briefing flag).
  TimelineIocsFlag:
    Description: Found directly in the evidence bundle (audit_token).
    Value: !Sub "TC{timeline-iocs-${FlagSeed}}"
  WafContainmentFlag:
    Description: Earned once the WAF rule is Block and the replayed attack returns 403.
    Value: !Sub "TC{waf-containment-${FlagSeed}}"
  PatchedWorkloadFlag:
    Description: Earned once both root-cause settings hold under a direct replay.
    Value: !Sub "TC{patched-workload-${FlagSeed}}"
  PersistenceRemovalFlag:
    Description: Earned once the rogue admin, the persistence marker, and the modified file are all cleared.
    Value: !Sub "TC{persistence-removal-${FlagSeed}}"
  CredentialRotationFlag:
    Description: Earned once the salt is rotated and the old token no longer authenticates.
    Value: !Sub "TC{credential-rotation-${FlagSeed}}"
  EvidencePreservationFlag:
    Description: Earned as long as the original evidence object is intact.
    Value: !Sub "TC{evidence-preservation-${FlagSeed}}"
  UptimeLegitTrafficFlag:
    Description: Earned once the index, the normal feed, and a legitimate authenticated request all return 200.
    Value: !Sub "TC{uptime-and-legit-traffic-${FlagSeed}}"
  NamePrefix:
    Description: Common resource prefix this stack used.
    Value: !Ref NamePrefix
  ParticipantViewerRoleArn:
    Description: Role ARN competitors AssumeRole to access their own stack via AWS Console.
    Value: !GetAtt ParticipantViewerRole.Arn
